      "writtenOn": "2023-12-07T00:15:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure I will use a separate namespace and the same package.\n\nI think having multiple namespaces in the single flags.aconfig file is fine, since we have the demo doing this (development/samples/AconfigDemo/aconfig_demo_flags.aconfig). Here are also a few examples:\n- packages/apps/Nfc/flags/nfc_flags.aconfig\n- frameworks/base/core/java/android/hardware/biometrics/flags.aconfig\n\nAlso package name + flag name forms the unique ID of a flag as per https://yaqs.corp.google.com/eng/q/6623555902257496064, thus all flags with the same package should live in the same file to mitigate the risk of conflicts.\n\nAt the same time, would it be possible if I add the flag first instead of waiting for the file move? I\u0027m building a platform feature that needs to access the API and currently blocked by the flag. I would greatly appreciate your help in removing the blocker.",
